From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Sun, 15 Nov 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] domicile: the shell and apps are cross-origin isolated

A shell or an app module (APP-MODULES.md) runs as a program, so it is
cross-origin isolated with no COOP, COEP or Document-Isolation-Policy
header: `crossOriginIsolated` is true and SharedArrayBuffer exists, for
threaded wasm and tools such as the TypeScript service.

- ContentBrowserClient::IsCrossOriginIsolatedByEmbedder names the
  origins. ChromeContentBrowserClient answers with
  domicile::IsCrossOriginIsolatedOrigin: `domicile://shell` and
  `domicile://app-<id>`.
- NavigationRequest::ComputeCrossOriginIsolationKey isolates such a
  document as Document-Isolation-Policy does: its own process and a
  concrete isolation key. It sets no policy, so nothing the document
  loads is checked for CORP. `<webview>` pages are unaffected.

Verified: not built. This repository cannot build Chromium; the engine
job builds it on `crux`.
